description.narrative:
a)	Strategic Compliance Plan formulated and formally adopted by national constituents on 13/09/2022.
(b)	Questionnaires for inspection visits developed.
(c)	Inspection visits were already conducted in 32 textile industry enterprises and 21 sericulture enterprises.
 ILO provided technical support and organized  the capacity-building trainings on soft skills for labour inspectors in Uzbekistan (01/02/2022 till 03/06/2022) ;
ILO provided technical support to the formulation and implementation of a Strategic Compliance Plan by the Labour Inspectorate of Uzbekistan (since 28/02/2022), including the participation, as speaker, in several Strategic Compliance Planning workshops, with national tripartite constituents and other stakeholders ;
ILO technical specialist participated, as speaker, in the Strategic Compliance Task Team Meeting, aimed at updating the Strategic Compliance Plan of the Uzbekistan's State Labour Inspectorate following the results of the scouting inspection visits carried out to 32 textile industry enterprises and 21 sericulture enterprises, within the framework of the adopted ILO Strategic Compliance Planning approach ;
ILO provided technical inputs and recommendations to the OSH text of the Mobile App on labour and OSH rights for agricultural workers in Uzbekistan, to be developed by the "UN Joint Programme on Multi-faceted response to the food and energy emergency in Uzbekistan", implemented jointly by UNICEF, FAO and the ILO ;
Technical Specialist participated as trainer, in the training sessions on Soft Skills, for the State Labour Inspectors of Uzbekistan for around 50 labour inspections improved their capacity to enforce legal provisions by developing their competences and soft skills ;
